cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, cite it as below. If you use the published data under
  docs/data, cite the dataset and the papers listed under references, and carry the
  ethics statement reproduced in docs/data/LICENSE.md without modification.
type: software
title: "ecog-lakehouse: a governed lakehouse over public ECoG recordings"
abstract: >-
  Recordings from the Stanford ECoG library stored in three layers on Parquet, with data
  contracts, checks generated from a regulatory requirements table, a decodable lineage
  identifier on every record, four planted performance faults with their fixes and
  benchmarks, and a static page that reruns the checks in the browser with DuckDB-WASM.
authors:
  - family-names: Monteiro
    given-names: Alexandre
repository-code: "https://github.com/MrBisonte/ecog-lakehouse"
url: "https://mrbisonte.github.io/ecog-lakehouse/"
license: MIT
version: 0.0.1
keywords:
  - lakehouse
  - data governance
  - data contracts
  - data lineage
  - DuckDB
  - Parquet
  - electrocorticography
